hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3031","Narrated to us ‘Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm: narrated to us Ibn Wahb: he informed me Mālik, and Yūnus, and al-Layth, and Ibn Jurayj — all of them from Ibn Shihāb — from Sulaymān ibn Yasār that ‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Abbās (RA) informed him, saying:\nAl-Faḍl ibn ‘Abbās (RA) was the Prophet’s riding-companion (ﷺ) on the Day of Sacrifice. A woman from Khath‘am came to the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) seeking a legal ruling. Al-Faḍl began to look at her, and she at him, so the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) turned al-Faḍl’s face to the other side with his hand. She said, “O Messenger of Allāh, Allāh’s prescribed duty of pilgrimage has reached my father, an old man too weak to ride steadily. May I perform the pilgrimage on his behalf?”\nHe replied, “Yes.”\nThis occurred during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\nAl-Layth added: Ibn Shihāb narrated it to me from Sulaymān or Abū Salamah or both, from Ibn ‘Abbās (RA).\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"3032","Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Ala’, narrated to us Sufyan, who said: I heard al-Zuhri.\nAnd narrated to us al-Makhzumi, narrated to us Sufyan.\nAnd narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Khashram, informed us Ibn ‘Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn ‘Abbas (RA), that a woman from Khath‘am came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the morning of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr), with al-Fadl riding behind him. She said: “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon His servants, but my father has reached old age and is too weak to ride. Do you think it is permissible for me to perform Hajj on his behalf?”\nHe (ﷺ) said: “Yes.”\n\nIn the narration of al-Makhzumi, it was on the morning of ‘Arafah (Yawm al-Jam‘), and he did not mention “with al-Fadl riding behind him.” The wording of Ibn Khashram in the text is similar to that of ‘Abd al-Jabbar, except that he said: “Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?” and he (ﷺ) said: “Yes.”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
